## 3. Root Cause Analysis (RCA)

The Datadog composite monitor detected abnormal behavior on `prod-worker-02`, where CPU utilization exceeded 80% and the application error rate exceeded 5%.

The transaction correlation ID `TXN-88129-CORR` was used to trace the affected checkout transaction. The same correlation ID was searched in the production checkout logs to locate the corresponding ERROR event and stack trace.

The evidence indicates that the checkout transaction was failing in the Credit Card Checker flow. The simulated `CreditCardChecker500` fault generated checkout processing failures, which increased the application error rate and contributed to the Datadog alert.

## 4. Verification & Next Action

- **Second view in the same platform that confirms (with screenshot):** Datadog monitor details showing `prod-worker-02`, CPU utilization above 80%, error rate above 5%, and correlation ID `TXN-88129-CORR`. The corresponding transaction should also be verified using the matching checkout ERROR log and stack trace.

- **Recommended Action Item / Escalation:** Investigate the Credit Card Checker failure associated with `TXN-88129-CORR`, review the matching application stack trace, and remediate the failing checkout dependency. Continue monitoring CPU utilization and checkout error rate after remediation to confirm that both metrics return to normal levels.
